    "scenesThatPass": [
      "BETHANY: Then who is she?\nSERENDIPITY: Not who - what. I haven't always been part of the anthropomorphic club. I used to be an abstract.\nBETHANY: Now I'm really lost.",
      "BETHANY: You made them sing that song?\nSERENDIPITY: I offered them a solution out of the hole they dug for themselves. Thankfully, they took it.\nBETHANY: Are you kidding? Those two are so dense, they wouldn't get a good idea if it was given to them in a specially marked box.\nSERENDIPITY: Dense people are the most open to suggestion - it's vou so-called intelligent folks that have a hard time accepting a good idea.",
      "SERENDIPITY: And sick of watching incapable people take brilliant inspiration and turn out real trash.\nBETHANY: So what happened?\nSERENDIPITY: Writer's block.",
      "SERENDIPITY: I don't know what the big surprise is - women are the only gender that can create life, just like God created the universe. Who else but a m…\nBETHANY: ...mom. God, it makes sense.\nSERENDIPITY: Not really useful in my new line of work.",
      "BETHANY: You know about that?\nSERENDIPITY: I always knew that thing was a bad idea. Leave it to the Catholics to destroy existence."
    ]
  },
